   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div>What am I missing?</div></div></blockquote><div><br></div><div>A lot of defaults that<font face=\"courier new, monospace\"> cfa() </font>turns on but<font face=\"courier new, monospace\"> lavaan() </font>leaves off.  <font face=\"courier new, monospace\">cfa()</font> is just a wrapper around<font face=\"courier new, monospace\"> lavaan()</font>.  Check the call this way:</div><div><br></div><blockquote style=\"margin:0 0 0 40px;border:none;padding:0px\"><div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">fit &lt;- cfa(model = &#39;latent =~ ind1 + ind2 + ind3 + ind4&#39;, data = foo)</font></div></div><div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">fit@call</font></div></div></blockquote><div><br></div><div>Or this way:</div><div><br></div><blockquote style=\"margin:0 0 0 40px;border:none;padding:0px\"><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">lavInspect(fit, &quot;call&quot;)</font></div></blockquote><div><br></div><div><div style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:small\"><div style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13px\">Terrence D. Jorgensen</div><div style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13px\">Postdoctoral Researcher, Methods and Statistics</div><div style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13px\">Research Institute for Child Development and Education, the University of Amsterdam</div><div style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13px\">UvA web page: <a href=\"http://www.uva.nl/profile/t.d.jorgensen\" style=\"color:rgb(17,85,204)\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://www.uva.nl/profile/t.d.jorgensen&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792428244381000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1ES9h7fiU2QZxaCQnyRsmb\">http://www.uva.nl/profile/t.d.jorgensen</a></div><div><br></div></div></div><div><br></div><div><br></div></div>"
